  "instance_name": "islamophobia_stereotype",
  "label": "Islamophobia Stereotype",
  "description": "The stereotype that Muslim women are oppressed or that hijab-wearing women are not modern or fashionable is a common form of Islamophobia. The meme directly counters this by presenting a confident, stylish Muslim woman, thereby challenging the stereotype that hijab = modesty = outdated. The background knowledge required to understand the meme’s intent is the existence of this stereotype and the cultural resistance to it. The image uses fashion as a tool to subvert negative perceptions.",
